From bfa4b73e2da1f58d3ee8124a6eaa2d7afb0825b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 05:03:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-302 lever 9: MUL_MAT_ID expert gather for Q2_0 and every
 legacy / q8_1 MMVQ id type

The slot-major expert gather (one dispatch over every (token, slot), shared experts read while
in L2) covered only the five IQ types of the qwen4exp file. The served file's nine Q2_0
ffn_down_exps tensors (2.4 ms per 4-row verify) still ran the per-token dispatch loop, and so
did every legacy, K-quant and MXFP4 MoE file on either the f32 or the q8_1 MMVQ route.

- vulkan-shaders-gen: idg f32 variants for the legacy set (mul_mat_vec.comp), idg q8_1 variants
  for every q8_1 id type (mul_mat_vecq.comp), arrays declared for both.
- ggml-vulkan: the idg twins use the workgroup, rows and spec constants of each id pipeline,
  so a row's arithmetic does not change. GGML_ARIFI_MOE_GATHER_EXT=0 opts out (unset = ON);
  the gather notice prints "ext N".
- test-backend-ops: served-shape MUL_MAT_ID cases for Q2_0 (down) and Q4_0, Q8_0, Q4_K, Q5_K,
  Q6_K, MXFP4 (gate) at n 1..8, 16 experts.

Origin: lane-302
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED at commit; op gates + timing in cache/moe-gather-x1-lane/cells/cellT-*/SUMMARY.txt
---
